From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] service: retry mode service start during OpenRC transitions

usb-signaller starts an OpenRC one-shot mode service after it enables the
new configfs gadget. During a supervisor restart, the preceding mode service
teardown and the new gadget start can overlap. rc-service may return a
transient failure while the one-shot service is still completing, and
usb-signaller then deletes the just-created gadget and falls back to
Charging.

Retry only the start operation a bounded number of times, leaving stop
best-effort and unchanged. Once the one-shot service settles, the retry
returns success and the gadget remains available.

--- a/src/service.rs
+++ b/src/service.rs
@@ -46,7 +46,17 @@
 }
 
 pub fn service_start(service: &str) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
-    return service_run(service, "start");
+    let mut last_error = None;
+    for attempt in 0..8 {
+        match service_run(service, "start") {
+            Ok(()) => return Ok(()),
+            Err(error) => last_error = Some(error),
+        }
+        if attempt < 7 {
+            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_secs(5));
+        }
+    }
+    return Err(last_error.unwrap());
 }
 
 pub fn service_stop(service: &str) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
